Package: gsp-surround
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: all
Maintainer: @MAINTAINER@
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Depends: python3, python3-gi, gir1.2-gtk-4.0, gir1.2-adw-1 (>= 1.2), pipewire, pipewire-bin, pipewire-pulse, wireplumber, udev, systemd
Recommends: pkexec | policykit-1
Section: sound
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/Sudashiii/gsp-surround-linux
Description: Virtual 7.1 surround and EQ presets for GSP headsets
 Recreates what the Windows driver does for Sennheiser GSP gaming headsets
 on Linux: virtual 7.1 surround through a filter measured from the original
 driver, and the EQ presets (Off, Game, Music, eSports) of the headset dongle.
 Made for the GSP 350 and PipeWire.
 .
 After installing, open "GSP Surround" from the menu, go to the Setup tab and
 click "Set up". The filter file is downloaded once; no password is needed.
 .
 Not affiliated with, endorsed by or connected to Sennheiser, EPOS, Conexant
 or Dolby Laboratories.
